WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.710
So, now that you have a nice scaffold

00:00:02.720 --> 00:00:04.550
for your build, what is now the best way

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:06.310
for us to tweak this design? Because

00:00:06.320 --> 00:00:07.910
when you're actually building things for

00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:10.190
real, and you want to serve it so that

00:00:10.200 --> 00:00:12.590
it is actually professionally made for

00:00:12.600 --> 00:00:14.230
your client, you'll actually go into

00:00:14.240 --> 00:00:15.630
this and just make sure that what it's

00:00:15.640 --> 00:00:17.830
saying here is exactly what you want.

00:00:17.840 --> 00:00:19.910
And maybe even remove some elements that

00:00:19.920 --> 00:00:21.630
you might not need. Now, part of the

00:00:21.640 --> 00:00:23.910
problem with these agentic platforms is

00:00:23.920 --> 00:00:25.630
that they are all chat-based, right? So,

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:27.390
you always need to prompt your agent to

00:00:27.400 --> 00:00:29.270
just change this particular line, or

00:00:29.280 --> 00:00:30.670
let's say you want a piece of text or a

00:00:30.680 --> 00:00:32.550
section to be larger than it currently

00:00:32.560 --> 00:00:34.350
is. What a lot of people do is they just

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.470
open up Claude Code, and actually just

00:00:36.480 --> 00:00:38.910
give that feedback as a prompt. And I

00:00:38.920 --> 00:00:40.870
think that is very, very wasteful.

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:42.350
Because what you're basically just going

00:00:42.360 --> 00:00:44.590
to do there is, if you provide all of

00:00:44.600 --> 00:00:46.430
that feedback into the prompt, the usual

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.390
challenge with that is, number one, it

00:00:48.400 --> 00:00:51.350
is very token heavy, and number two, it

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:53.630
is often that Claude and any other

00:00:53.640 --> 00:00:55.830
agentic platform doesn't really know

00:00:55.840 --> 00:00:57.910
exactly what you need or want,

00:00:57.920 --> 00:00:59.670
especially when it comes to matters of

00:00:59.680 --> 00:01:01.950
visual taste. So, how I approach this is

00:01:01.960 --> 00:01:04.070
I develop a skill called slash tweak.

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:05.830
And what I'm saying here is I just want

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:07.750
to apply a slash tweak panel in the

00:01:07.760 --> 00:01:10.150
page, and to give me at least 15

00:01:10.160 --> 00:01:11.710
sliders. So, you'll see in a bit what

00:01:11.720 --> 00:01:13.390
this will do. Because what this tweak

00:01:13.400 --> 00:01:15.870
skill does is it just introduces this

00:01:15.880 --> 00:01:17.710
slider on the right, which you can

00:01:17.720 --> 00:01:19.350
obviously just drag around. And what

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:21.830
this does is it just lets you adjust or

00:01:21.840 --> 00:01:24.070
tweak things to your liking. So, let's

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:26.550
say you want the text to be bigger or

00:01:26.560 --> 00:01:29.310
smaller, you can just adjust this slider

00:01:29.320 --> 00:01:31.470
in order to You can also make the labels

00:01:31.480 --> 00:01:32.910
smaller or bigger. And if you remember

00:01:32.920 --> 00:01:34.510
the prompt that I sent is I want at

00:01:34.520 --> 00:01:35.990
least 15 sliders, you can actually

00:01:36.000 --> 00:01:38.110
control this. So, if this is a more

00:01:38.120 --> 00:01:40.510
complex build, and you want more sliders

00:01:40.520 --> 00:01:42.510
or you want more specific sliders, then

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.230
you'll be able to just invoke that just

00:01:44.240 --> 00:01:45.950
by telling Claude to do it. So, usually

00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:47.830
when I'm designing a build, I just add

00:01:47.840 --> 00:01:49.830
this tweak skill, and I just play around

00:01:49.840 --> 00:01:51.990
with these sliders in order to get the

00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:53.590
actual look that I want. And the other

00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:55.270
thing that is important here is if you

00:01:55.280 --> 00:01:57.030
want to edit any of the text, you can

00:01:57.040 --> 00:01:59.230
actually just click on edit in here. And

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.230
once you're on edit mode on, let's say

00:02:01.240 --> 00:02:02.830
you want to change this piece of text

00:02:02.840 --> 00:02:04.390
from the questions everyone actually

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.630
asks to let's say we want that to begin

00:02:06.640 --> 00:02:08.389
with FAQ, the questions everyone

00:02:08.399 --> 00:02:10.550
actually asks. We can do that as well.

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.710
So, let's say we want to change this

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:13.830
from honest metrics to honest pricing

00:02:13.840 --> 00:02:15.590
upfront. We can do that as well straight

00:02:15.600 --> 00:02:16.790
in the page. The other thing that is

00:02:16.800 --> 00:02:19.230
useful here is this remove button. And

00:02:19.240 --> 00:02:20.870
if I click on that, then I'll be able to

00:02:20.880 --> 00:02:22.990
just point to any element here on the

00:02:23.000 --> 00:02:25.190
page and I'll be able to remove them.

00:02:25.200 --> 00:02:27.270
So, let's see. So, let's say in this FAQ

00:02:27.280 --> 00:02:29.150
section, we want to remove question

00:02:29.160 --> 00:02:30.990
number six, we want to remove question

00:02:31.000 --> 00:02:33.790
number four, that is possible as well.

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:35.030
And when you're done with that, all you

00:02:35.040 --> 00:02:37.350
need to do is to click copy all and that

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:38.510
will just copy a prompt to your

00:02:38.520 --> 00:02:40.070
clipboard that we can now go back to

00:02:40.080 --> 00:02:42.750
Claude and send it to bake all of those

00:02:42.760 --> 00:02:45.550
changes to your final front-end design.

00:02:45.560 --> 00:02:47.030
And after a few seconds, and now it's

00:02:47.040 --> 00:02:49.670
done tweaking that. And you can see that

00:02:49.680 --> 00:02:51.190
this piece of text, that's now much

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.230
larger. This headline now changed to

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:55.390
honest pricing upfront. And basically

00:02:55.400 --> 00:02:57.750
all of the changes that we baked now has

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.550
been applied to the final front-end

00:02:59.560 --> 00:03:02.270
design. So, that is a great way for you

00:03:02.280 --> 00:03:04.630
to just stop sending prompts every time

00:03:04.640 --> 00:03:06.509
you need to make a change because more

00:03:06.519 --> 00:03:08.390
often than not in matters of visual

00:03:08.400 --> 00:03:10.550
taste, especially in the final stages

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:12.590
when you're just tweaking it to remove

00:03:12.600 --> 00:03:14.830
or edit elements, it is much better to

00:03:14.840 --> 00:03:17.030
use that tweak skill in order to arrive

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.670
at the final look and feel that you want

00:03:19.680 --> 00:03:22.239
to have.
